# ops/agentd/mint.service — reference systemd --user unit for agentd on MINT,
# the always-on browser host.
#
# This is the CANONICAL copy. The live unit lives at
#   ~/.config/systemd/user/agentd.service
# on the always-on host; keep the two byte-identical. `ops/agentd/deploy.sh --check` diffs
# the live unit against this file and fails on drift.
#
# MINT vs AVALANCHE — why a second unit rather than one shared file:
# source/src/config.ts is deliberately PORTABLE; every box-specific value is an
# Environment= override here rather than a hard-code back in config.ts. the always-on host
# differs from the workstation in more than paths, so the overrides are worth reading
# rather than skimming:
#
#   AGENTD_ALWAYS_ON         the always-on host NEVER sleeps — it hosts the FRIDAY kiosk,
#                            Firecrawl, Home Assistant, searxng, mealie,
#                            matter-server and mosquitto. The whole WoL / drain
#                            / suspend state machine is not just unused but
#                            actively dangerous here (`systemctl suspend` would
#                            take the household stack down). This unarms the
#                            drain ticker and makes /wake-ack a 409.
#                            THIS is the power win: no workstation POST+resume
#                            cycle per scrape, and no discrete GPU spinning up
#                            in a house that evacuates heat slowly.
#
#   AGENTD_COMPOSITOR_*      the always-on host runs GNOME, so kwin_wayland is not native and
#                            `apt install kwin-wayland` would drag in 461
#                            packages of Plasma. Weston's headless backend is
#                            10 packages and gives the same nested, invisible
#                            output — with HARDWARE GL, which is the part that
#                            actually matters (verified on this box):
#                              GL vendor:   AMD
#                              GL renderer: AMD Radeon Graphics
#                                           (radeonsi, gfx1151, LLVM 20.1.2)
#                            gfx1151 is the integrated AI accelerator. A software (llvmpipe)
#                            renderer string would be precisely the bot signal
#                            this whole surface exists to avoid, so if you ever
#                            change these args, re-verify the renderer.
#                            --idle-time=0 stops weston idling out mid-session.
#
#   AGENTD_FIREFOX_BINARY    the always-on host's distro Firefox is a SNAP. Snap confinement
#   AGENTD_GECKODRIVER_*     blocks both halves of what agentd needs: opening a
#                            profile at an arbitrary path, and reaching the
#                            per-session Wayland socket in XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. So
#                            both binaries are unconfined Mozilla builds under
#                            ~/opt. Firefox is pinned to the SAME version as
#                            the workstation (152.0.5) on purpose — a profile opened
#                            by a newer Firefox cannot be reopened by an older
#                            one, and the two hosts share migrated profiles, so
#                            a one-sided upgrade would strand the fallback.
#                            Bump BOTH boxes together.
#
#   AGENTD_SESSION_BLOCKERS  The default set models a workstation ("is Jasper at
#                            his desk"). the always-on host is a headless server: nobody sits
#                            at it, and `external_ssh` — a default blocker —
#                            would stall an in-turn browse for as long as any
#                            admin stayed logged in. What genuinely contends
#                            here is RAM (31 GiB system, since 96 of the 128 is
#                            carved out to the iGPU) and package-manager locks.
#
#   AGENTD_MAX_SESSIONS      v1 serialized to one session globally; a second
#                            agent got a 503. Fine when only Maggie browsed,
#                            wrong now that Kate uses browse_url as her in-turn
#                            web_fetch_clean failover — she would collide with
#                            any background scrape. 32 threads and an idle iGPU
#                            carry 3 comfortably.
#
# If you change a box-specific value, change it HERE and re-run
# `deploy.sh --check` — do not reintroduce the value into config.ts.
#
# NB no After=graphical-session.target (the workstation has one): agentd on the always-on host is
# fully headless and must come up without any seat session. `loginctl
# enable-linger jasper` is what keeps this user manager — and /run/user/1000,
# where the session sockets live — alive across logouts and reboots.
[Unit]
Description=Hearth agentd — LAN browser daemon (always-on host)

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/bun run /home/jasper/hearthoperator/agentd/src/main.ts
WorkingDirectory=/home/jasper/hearthoperator/agentd
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=3
Environment="AGENTD_PORT=4446"
Environment="AGENTD_BIND=0.0.0.0"
Environment="AGENTD_TOKEN_FILE=/home/jasper/.config/agentd/token"
Environment="AGENTD_ACTIVITY_SCRIPT=/home/jasper/hearthoperator/bin/mint-activity.sh"
Environment="AGENTD_FIREFOX_PROFILE_BASE=/home/jasper/.mozilla/firefox"
Environment="AGENTD_ALWAYS_ON=1"
Environment="AGENTD_MAX_SESSIONS=3"
Environment="AGENTD_PUBLIC_HOST=192.168.0.62"
Environment="AGENTD_COMPOSITOR_CMD=weston"
Environment="AGENTD_COMPOSITOR_ARGS=--backend=headless --renderer=gl --width={width} --height={height} --xwayland --socket={socket} --idle-time=0"
Environment="AGENTD_FIREFOX_BINARY=/home/jasper/opt/firefox/firefox"
Environment="AGENTD_GECKODRIVER_BINARY=/home/jasper/opt/bin/geckodriver"
Environment="AGENTD_GECKODRIVER_PATH=/home/jasper/opt/bin:/home/jasper/opt/firefox:/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin"
Environment="AGENTD_SESSION_BLOCKERS=memory_pressure,package_manager_running"
# Tunables intentionally not pinned via Environment= so they can be overridden
# with `systemctl --user set-environment ...` during tests. Drain/suspend are
# absent on purpose — AGENTD_ALWAYS_ON makes them unreachable.
PassEnvironment=AGENTD_MIN_AVAIL_MB AGENTD_IDLE_THRESHOLD_SECONDS AGENTD_DEBUG

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
